# HabitFlow Multi-Theme & Color Palette System (Settings Picker — Zero-Breakage Implementation)

## 1. Objective
Extend HabitFlow's existing **Obsidian & Mint** design system (`src/app/globals.css`, `src/providers/theme-provider.tsx`, `src/components/settings/SettingsPageContent.tsx`) so users can switch between **6 curated, non-generic, full-surface Theme Palettes** AND optionally customize their **Accent Color** directly from **Settings → Appearance** — with instant live preview, zero flash of unstyled content (FOUC), and **100% backward compatibility** so zero existing pages, charts, sync pipelines, or unit tests break.

---

## 2. Hard Guardrails ("Nothing Must Break")
1. **Zero Breaking Changes to Existing Exports:**
   - Keep `ThemeProvider` and `useTheme()` in `src/providers/theme-provider.tsx` exporting all existing properties (`theme`, `setTheme`, `resolvedTheme`, and if present `accent`, `setAccent`).
   - Add new properties cleanly alongside them: `colorTheme`, `setColorTheme`, `accentOverride`, `setAccentOverride`, `resetAppearance`.
   - Do **NOT** change the `ThemeProvider` props signature or mock structure expected by `src/app/__tests__/layout.test.tsx`.
2. **Zero Database / Sync Breakage:**
   - Do **NOT** require a new Supabase SQL migration or alter Dexie schema versions. Persist `habitflow_color_theme` and `habitflow_accent_override` in `localStorage` (alongside existing `theme`), with graceful fallbacks if keys are missing, corrupted, or contain legacy values (e.g., migrate legacy `theme: 'auto'` -> `'system'`).
3. **Zero Hydration Warnings:**
   - Keep `suppressHydrationWarning` on `<html>` in `src/app/layout.tsx`.
   - Keep all interactive theme cards in `SettingsPageContent.tsx` guarded by `mounted` so SSR and client initial render match cleanly.
4. **Preserve Semantic Status Clarity Across ALL Themes:**
   - Every theme MUST keep `--success` (completed habits / income / under-budget), `--rest` (Rest Days / transfers), `--warning` (pace warnings / due soon), `--destructive` (over-budget / overdue / delete), and `--invest` (SIPs / XP / AI) clearly legible and distinct from the theme's surfaces.
   - Maintain **WCAG AA contrast (`>= 4.5:1`)** for `--foreground` on `--background`/`--card`, `--muted-foreground` on `--card`, and `--primary-foreground` on `--primary` in BOTH Light and Dark modes for every single theme.
5. **Preserve Existing Typography & 3-Tier Surfaces:**
   - Do NOT touch `Geist` / `Geist Mono` fonts, `.surface-hero`, `.surface-card`, `.surface-subtle`, `.surface-chrome`, or any layout spacing/functionality across Dashboard, Habits, Tasks, Goals, Finance, or Analytics.

---

## 3. Architecture: 3 Independent Layers of Appearance

Separate appearance into three clean, orthogonal controls:

1. **Surface Brightness (`theme`):** `'light' | 'dark' | 'system'` -> applies `.light` or `.dark` class on `<html>`.
2. **Theme Palette (`colorTheme`):** Applied via `data-theme="<id>"` on `<html>`. Defines BOTH the **Light & Dark background/card/border/muted surface tone** AND the **default primary/accent/chart colors** for that theme:
   - `'obsidian-mint'` *(Default)* — **Obsidian & Mint** (Crisp Alabaster / Pure Graphite Obsidian + Refined Mint)
   - `'warm-stone-forest'` — **Warm Stone & Forest** (Warm Paper / Deep Espresso-Charcoal + Forest Green & subtle warm accents)
   - `'monochrome-cobalt'` — **Monochrome Ink + Cobalt** (Pure White / Pitch Zinc + High-Contrast Ink buttons & Electric Cobalt focus/rings/charts)
   - `'nordic-amber'` — **Nordic Slate & Amber** (Cool Mist / Deep Architectural Slate + Burnished Warm Amber)
   - `'sandstone-terracotta'` — **Sandstone & Terracotta** (Soft Linen Cream / Deep Warm Umber + Earthy Clay Terracotta)
   - `'deep-sea-cyan'` — **Deep Sea & Cyan** (Crisp Ice White / Abyssal Navy-Graphite + Clear Glacier Cyan)
3. **Accent Color Override (`accentOverride`):** Applied via `data-accent="<id>"` on `<html>` ONLY when not `'theme'`.
   - Values: `'theme'` *(Match Theme — default)* | `'mint'` | `'forest'` | `'cobalt'` | `'amber'` | `'terracotta'` | `'cyan'` | `'ink'`
   - Declared **AFTER** all `[data-theme="..."]` rules in `src/app/globals.css` so it cleanly overrides ONLY `--primary`, `--primary-foreground`, `--accent`, `--accent-foreground`, `--ring`, and `--chart-1` while keeping the chosen theme's Light/Dark surface palette intact!

