## 4. Create Single Source of Truth Metadata (`src/lib/themes.ts`)

Create a lightweight, typed metadata file `src/lib/themes.ts` exporting:
- `ColorThemeId` union type (`'obsidian-mint' | 'warm-stone-forest' | 'monochrome-cobalt' | 'nordic-amber' | 'sandstone-terracotta' | 'deep-sea-cyan'`)
- `AccentOverrideId` union type (`'theme' | 'mint' | 'forest' | 'cobalt' | 'amber' | 'terracotta' | 'cyan' | 'ink'`)
- `COLOR_THEMES`: array of objects for each of the 6 themes containing:
  - `id: ColorThemeId`
  - `name: string` (e.g., `"Obsidian & Mint"`)
  - `tagline: string` (short 3–5 word vibe, e.g., `"Fintech calm · Graphite & Mint"`)
  - `lightPreview`: `{ bg, card, border, primary, secondary }` (exact CSS color strings for rendering rich mini UI swatch cards in Settings)
  - `darkPreview`: `{ bg, card, border, primary, secondary }`
  - `themeColorLight: string` and `themeColorDark: string` (hex values so `ThemeProvider` can dynamically update `<meta name="theme-color">` on mobile browsers/PWA!)
- `ACCENT_OVERRIDES`: array of `{ id: AccentOverrideId; label: string; swatchLight: string; swatchDark: string }`
- Helper validators `isValidColorTheme(val)` and `isValidAccentOverride(val)`.

